rror tables (specs/cli.md:251-263 and 267-275) map 126 only to \"Command blocked by the interruptor\" - the bridge-unavailable case has no row. (2) Seccomp activation claims: specs/cli.md:80 says --seccomp is \"Equivalent to TERMINAL_JAIL_SECCOMP=1; the env var controls the default\", :127 requires usage text \"Controlled by TERMINAL_JAIL_SECCOMP env var (default off)\", and :171 says the env var \"enables the same path without the flag\". Live: the wrapper never READS the variable - USE_SECCOMP is hardcoded 0 and only the --seccomp case sets 1; grep of standalone/terminal-jail finds the name only as an outbound export for the loader (L379) and in help text that states the opposite (L63-64). Discriminating probe: TERMINAL_JAIL_SECCOMP=1 TERMINAL_JAIL_SECCOMP_LOADER=<missing path> ./standalone/terminal-jail --user echo env-var-only -> \"env-var-only\" rc=0 (the loader is never resolved, so the variable activated nothing), while the same run WITH --seccomp exits 2 naming the missing loader. A user exporting the variable believes syscall filtering is on and gets none. (3) The spec never mentions TERMINAL_JAIL_SECCOMP_LOADER, the loader-path override the wrapper really reads (L23)."}
