 {"status": "complete", "id": "VERSION-002", "title": "LOAD-HYGIENE: bound test-suite host load (audit tests for parallel-spawn / per-assertion subprocess / unbounded-loop patterns; fix the worst offender with bounded waves or in-process coverage; keep full-suite coverage; NO skip-gates, NO fleet-scheduling changes) — fleet pattern evidence: task-router TR-077/TR-078 2026-09-19 (40-at-once interpreter stampede, 66 seed builds/run, full core)", "priority": "P2", "detail": "Fleet directive (Bane, criterion 7 of the 2026-09-19 retirement loop): 1-2 projects must not eat the whole box's CPU; the foreman also won't run next processes under excess load. Proven fleet pattern from task-router 2026-09-19: a concurrency test fired 40 simultaneous interpreter spawns (fixed: bounded waves of 8, same contract, TR-078); a suite built 66 private seed registries per run (fixed: one shared session build for read-only consumers, private builds kept where inputs mutate, TR-077); missing pandas in a venv turned every seed into a full-core burn for minutes. ACCEPTANCE (audit-then-fix, in-repo only): (1) audit this repo's test suite for the three patterns: (a) tests spawning >8 concurrent subprocesses, (b) a subprocess per assertion where the process boundary is not the subject under test, (c) loops re-running an expensive builder per test when one shared build would cover read-only assertions; (2) fix the single WORST offender found (bound waves with an env knob clamped 2-16, or in-process + one real-exec parity smoke, or a session-scoped shared fixture + per-test copy); do NOT time-box, cache, or skip tests to pass; do NOT change fleet/scheduler concurrency policy (owner-set); (3) prove before/after with a concrete measurement (spawn count, wall clock, or peak concurrent children) recorded in the completion event; (4) full regression suite green after the change (in-flight runs are not passed). REFERENCE: task-router tests/conftest.py (shared_seed_registry/seed_registry_copy) and tests